# SEND-SITE-ARTIFICIAL-CAPS (Codex, 2026-09-30): letters of more fields than the 16 a site held -- a method's
# of twenty-four (x * j + j, every sixth from the third a text) and the root's of twenty (b + 10 j, every fifth a
# text), then the exit.  The driver's `postlog 1` says each post, its fields in order.
fn: wide (int: x) int
    sendMessage: letter(f1: x * 1 + 1; f2: x * 2 + 2; t3: "m3"; f4: x * 4 + 4; f5: x * 5 + 5; f6: x * 6 + 6; f7: x * 7 + 7; f8: x * 8 + 8; t9: "m9"; f10: x * 10 + 10; f11: x * 11 + 11; f12: x * 12 + 12; f13: x * 13 + 13; f14: x * 14 + 14; t15: "m15"; f16: x * 16 + 16; f17: x * 17 + 17; f18: x * 18 + 18; f19: x * 19 + 19; f20: x * 20 + 20; t21: "m21"; f22: x * 22 + 22; f23: x * 23 + 23; f24: x * 24 + 24)
    return: 0
end: wide

int: b 2
wide(b + 1)
sendMessage: root(g1: b + 10; g2: b + 20; g3: b + 30; g4: b + 40; t5: "r5"; g6: b + 60; g7: b + 70; g8: b + 80; g9: b + 90; t10: "r10"; g11: b + 110; g12: b + 120; g13: b + 130; g14: b + 140; t15: "r15"; g16: b + 160; g17: b + 170; g18: b + 180; g19: b + 190; t20: "r20")
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
